cff-version: 1.2.0

title: "Benchmarking Fault-Tolerance Characteristics of Actor-Based Runtimes"

message: >
  If you use this benchmark framework or any part of its implementation
  in your research, please cite both this repository and the accompanying
  publication.

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Nogueira"
    given-names: "Luís"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7094-0458"

  - family-names: "Coelho"
    given-names: "Jorge"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3395-6426"

repository-code: "https://github.com/lmpnogueira/actor-fault-tolerance-benchmark"

license: MIT

abstract: >
  A language-independent benchmarking framework for evaluating the
  fault-tolerance characteristics of actor-based runtimes through
  equivalent benchmark implementations in Elixir/BEAM, Scala/Akka,
  and Go/Proto.Actor. The repository constitutes the complete
  replication package accompanying the published article.

keywords:
  - actor model
  - actor systems
  - distributed systems
  - fault tolerance
  - benchmarking
  - fault injection
  - supervised recovery
  - Elixir
  - BEAM
  - Scala
  - Akka
  - Go
  - Proto.Actor

